    {
      "id": "5f836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements &amp; Admissions deadlines See approved General Education courses at CSU Fullerton. See Associate Degree for Transfer. See the Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP) .",
      "contentHtml": "<blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the Admissions website for </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/prospectivestudent/transferlocaladmissionarea.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">transfer admission requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> &amp; </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/deadlines/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Admissions deadlines</a></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.fullerton.edu/undergraduate/general-education/approved-courses.html#box5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">approved General Education </a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">courses at CSU Fullerton. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/associate-degree-for-transfer-major-and-campus-search.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Associate Degree for Transfer.</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/external-exams/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP)</a><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/student-services/casper/Pages/external-exam-credit.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">.</a></blockquote>"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3806f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About This Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bb806f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "(120 UNITS) The Bachelor of Arts in Communications ( Link ) provides students with training in the theory and practice of informing, instructing and persuading through communications media. Because effective ethical communications are essential for the well-being of a democratic society, the curriculum ensures that all majors are: exposed to a broad liberal education; provided with a clear understanding and a global perspective of the role of communications media in society; and prepared for communications-related careers in the mass media, business, government and education by educating them in depth on one of the specialized concentrations within the department. The program includes 24 units of core requirements and 21 units (45 units total) in a chosen concentration. Students must also complete a minimum of 12 units, earned through: a Department of Communications certificate; a minor outside the department; or approved coursework outside the department. In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree section in this catalog for complete information. All Department of Communications prerequisite courses must be completed with a “C” (2.0) or better. Concentration The Advertising concentration ( Link ) provides students with the knowledge to plan and develop consumer-focused media campaigns. They learn to blend creative strategy and execution with consumer and market research to aid with promoting and selling products and services in such positions as account executive, brand manager, copywriter, digital media specialist, graphic designer, interactive producer and social media analyst. A total of 21 units within the concentration are required, which include required courses (6 units), a principles course (3), elective courses (6 units), an upper-division writing course (3 units), and a capstone course (3). IMPORTANT: The Accrediting Council on Education in Journalism and Mass Communications has set forth strict guidelines for majors in communications. It is imperative that you see the CSU Fullerton catalog under \"Department of Communications,\" \"Bachelor of Arts in Communications\" for additional requirements ( Link ).",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>(120&nbsp;UNITS)</strong></p><p>The&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;in&nbsp;Communications&nbsp;(<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_entity.php?catoid=101&amp;ent_oid=11324&amp;returnto=15143\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)&nbsp;provides&nbsp;students&nbsp;with&nbsp;training&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;theory&nbsp;and&nbsp;practice&nbsp;of&nbsp;informing,&nbsp;instructing&nbsp;and&nbsp;persuading&nbsp;through&nbsp;communications&nbsp;media.&nbsp;Because&nbsp;effective&nbsp;ethical&nbsp;communications&nbsp;are&nbsp;essential&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;well-being&nbsp;of&nbsp;a&nbsp;democratic&nbsp;society,&nbsp;the&nbsp;curriculum&nbsp;ensures&nbsp;that&nbsp;all&nbsp;majors&nbsp;are:&nbsp;exposed&nbsp;to&nbsp;a&nbsp;broad&nbsp;liberal&nbsp;education;&nbsp;provided&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;clear&nbsp;understanding&nbsp;and&nbsp;a&nbsp;global&nbsp;perspective&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;role&nbsp;of&nbsp;communications&nbsp;media&nbsp;in&nbsp;society;&nbsp;and&nbsp;prepared&nbsp;for&nbsp;communications-related&nbsp;careers&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;mass&nbsp;media,&nbsp;business,&nbsp;government&nbsp;and&nbsp;education&nbsp;by&nbsp;educating&nbsp;them&nbsp;in&nbsp;depth&nbsp;on&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;specialized&nbsp;concentrations&nbsp;within&nbsp;the&nbsp;department.</p><p></p><p>The&nbsp;program&nbsp;includes&nbsp;24&nbsp;units&nbsp;of&nbsp;core&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;and&nbsp;21&nbsp;units&nbsp;(45&nbsp;units&nbsp;total)&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;chosen&nbsp;concentration.&nbsp;Students&nbsp;must&nbsp;also&nbsp;complete&nbsp;a&nbsp;minimum&nbsp;of&nbsp;12&nbsp;units,&nbsp;earned&nbsp;through:&nbsp;a&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Communications&nbsp;certificate;&nbsp;a&nbsp;minor&nbsp;outside&nbsp;the&nbsp;department;&nbsp;or&nbsp;approved&nbsp;coursework&nbsp;outside&nbsp;the&nbsp;department.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>In&nbsp;addition&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;major,&nbsp;students&nbsp;must&nbsp;meet&nbsp;all&nbsp;other&nbsp;university&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;bachelor’s&nbsp;degree.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;consult&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/content.php?catoid=101&amp;navoid=15099\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Graduation&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor’s&nbsp;Degree</a>&nbsp;section&nbsp;in&nbsp;this&nbsp;catalog&nbsp;for&nbsp;complete&nbsp;information.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>All&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Communications&nbsp;prerequisite&nbsp;courses&nbsp;must&nbsp;be&nbsp;completed&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;“C”&nbsp;(2.0)&nbsp;or&nbsp;better.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p><strong>Concentration</strong></p><p>The&nbsp;Advertising&nbsp;concentration&nbsp;(<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=101&amp;poid=47234&amp;returnto=15143\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)&nbsp;provides&nbsp;students&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;to&nbsp;plan&nbsp;and&nbsp;develop&nbsp;consumer-focused&nbsp;media&nbsp;campaigns.&nbsp;They&nbsp;learn&nbsp;to&nbsp;blend&nbsp;creative&nbsp;strategy&nbsp;and&nbsp;execution&nbsp;with&nbsp;consumer&nbsp;and&nbsp;market&nbsp;research&nbsp;to&nbsp;aid&nbsp;with&nbsp;promoting&nbsp;and&nbsp;selling&nbsp;products&nbsp;and&nbsp;services&nbsp;in&nbsp;such&nbsp;positions&nbsp;as&nbsp;account&nbsp;executive,&nbsp;brand&nbsp;manager,&nbsp;copywriter,&nbsp;digital&nbsp;media&nbsp;specialist,&nbsp;graphic&nbsp;designer,&nbsp;interactive&nbsp;producer&nbsp;and&nbsp;social&nbsp;media&nbsp;analyst.</p><p></p><p>A&nbsp;total&nbsp;of&nbsp;21&nbsp;units&nbsp;within&nbsp;the&nbsp;concentration&nbsp;are&nbsp;required,&nbsp;which&nbsp;include&nbsp;required&nbsp;courses&nbsp;(6&nbsp;units),&nbsp;a&nbsp;principles&nbsp;course&nbsp;(3),&nbsp;elective&nbsp;courses&nbsp;(6&nbsp;units),&nbsp;an&nbsp;upper-division&nbsp;writing&nbsp;course&nbsp;(3&nbsp;units),&nbsp;and&nbsp;a&nbsp;capstone&nbsp;course&nbsp;(3).&nbsp;IMPORTANT:&nbsp;The&nbsp;Accrediting&nbsp;Council&nbsp;on&nbsp;Education&nbsp;in&nbsp;Journalism&nbsp;and&nbsp;Mass&nbsp;Communications&nbsp;has&nbsp;set&nbsp;forth&nbsp;strict&nbsp;guidelines&nbsp;for&nbsp;majors&nbsp;in&nbsp;communications.&nbsp;It&nbsp;is&nbsp;imperative&nbsp;that&nbsp;you&nbsp;see&nbsp;the&nbsp;CSU&nbsp;Fullerton&nbsp;catalog&nbsp;under&nbsp;\"Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Communications,\"&nbsp;\"Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;in&nbsp;Communications\"&nbsp;for&nbsp;additional&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;(<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_entity.php?catoid=101&amp;ent_oid=11324&amp;returnto=15143\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>).</p>"
    },
